              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LOVECED"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I served this with white rice and the whole family loved it--it was quick and easy but SO tasty!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GRAMMA GORGEOUS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe needs spice changes to meet our taste. Chicken, celery, onion and soy sauce are a good start, but we prefer to use sesame oil, water chestnuts not mushrooms, and some chicken broth not water, 1/4 tsp. garlic powder and pinch of Chinese 5 spice then tighten the sauce up with a Tb. or less of cornstarch. Serve on cooked rice, pass the soy sauce, and top with crunchy Chinese noodles.",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-07T08:58:24.490Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RMSR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used fresh mushrooms and replaced the 'mushroom' liquid I would've had from the can with 2 TBsps. 'Mama Sita's BBQ Marinade/Sauce'. This helped mellow out the soy/salty flavour. I also added fresh garlic, red belle peppers, green bell peppers and sliced carrots. Served over rice.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-25T10:57:20.750Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ZAKKIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Of the 3 adults (kid wouldn't try it) at the table, 2 gave it a 3 (not enough taste, not attractive) and 1 gave it a 5. It was too watery so if I make it next time, I will drain the mushrooms. I would also add a touch of cornstarch to the soy sauce to make more of a coating for the chicken and veggies. Garnishing with chopped green onions would help with the appearance.",
            "datePublished": "2008-07-19T11:11:02.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Liz Olmanson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so good. I did add a red pepper and also real mushrooms and some chicken broth. I was so surprised that this was so tasty. I will make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2014-10-03T09:03:05.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sandy Beckwith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really is wonderful....like a previous reviewer, it is not very appealing to the eye. I followed a few others reviews and altered the recipe. I used FRESH mushrooms, did not use 3 onions, because I only had one...cannot imagine using 3..maybe 2, but not 3.. I added some cabbage, and on my next time of cooking this (it is good enough for me to cook again) I am going to add water chestnuts for crunch and flavor. On the pic you see something red, so will try red bell pepper. If I can cook something and everyone loves it, A OK with me!",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-25T00:14:09.537Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Rose Stumphf"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really easy and fast. Easily adapting any asian vegetables that you may want to add. I added a can of bean sprouts, substituted sesame oil, and added extra chicken.",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-11T11:37:57.960Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pam Ziegler Lutz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good and simple enough. I used fresh mushrooms and a little bit of chicken broth to replace the mushroom liquid. The finished dish isn’t the prettiest to look at. It would benefit from some added color. If I make this again, I would probably add some red and green peppers.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-06T17:54:19.497Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This reminds me so much of a dish my mom would make growing up. Super simple for quick weeknight dinners. Served over rice, the taste is reminiscent of fried rice. The only thing I’d change is the method. Chicken does not need that long to simmer, and at risk of overcooking the chicken but still getting the celery done in time, I suggest the following - saute the chicken and celery together from the start, then add in the onion and mushrooms and simmer for about 8-10 minutes. There’s not much liquid in this dish, so if you want extra to serve over rice, add in some broth or water.",
            "datePublished": "2022-06-14T19:03:18.354Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Katy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good. Simple easy. My husband who is very picky likes it. So now it’s on my regular repertoire and keep canned mushrooms in the pantry.",
